1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,380
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:23,520
I kick a pebble,
and it flies all the way there,

3
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:29,180
landing right on the gym teacher's head.

4
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:11,040
Thank you for watching.

5
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:27,420
A little while ago

6
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:34,020
Kameari has changed quite a bit since the old days,
hasn't it.

7
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:38,600
Back when I graduated from the
police academy and was assigned here,

8
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,900
the line wasn't elevated yet.

9
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:43,680
There was a large freight yard.

10
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,160
There were a few factories too.

11
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:51,340
The population was growing,
and the downtown area kept expanding.

12
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:53,780
There were five movie theaters, you know!

13
00:01:56,980 --> 00:02:00,280
If I remember right, there was a
tobacco shop just around this corner,

14
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:08,220
So Yoko-chan's tobacco shop is gone too.

15
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:09,160
Yoko-chan?

16
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:10,554
Oh, right.

17
00:02:10,604 --> 00:02:15,100
The tobacco shop that was here
had a shop girl named Yoko-chan.

18
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:17,800
That was over ten years ago now, I suppose.

19
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:22,880
Hey, old lady, hey, old lady!

20
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:31,740
Tsk, what a pain. Let's see, it should
be stashed around here like always.

21
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,700
Aaaaaah!

22
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:39,100
Eeeeeeh!

23
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,640
Aaaaaah!

24
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:45,560
Thief!

25
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,340
I'm not a thief!

26
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,260
I'm a police officer.

27
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:52,020
A thief pretending to be a cop

28
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:52,780
No.

29
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:55,120
I just came to buy cigarettes.

30
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,060
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

31
00:02:58,060 --> 00:02:59,580
Hey, old lady.

32
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:01,120
Grandma.

33
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,660
Talk to me, Yone.

34
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:05,120
Hey, you're making that face, though.

35
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,760
He's a real police officer.

36
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:07,960
Real.

37
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:10,320
I'm sorry.

38
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,380
I thought for sure

39
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:15,360
W-well, I was wrong to try to grab
the cigarettes without permission too.

40
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,920
Still, you threw me beautifully.

41
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,760
That was a full ippon, no doubt about it.

42
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,000
Well, of course.

43
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,140
That girl is my granddaughter.
Her name's Yoko.

44
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,900
She did judo in middle school, you know.

45
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,920
O-oh, I see. No wonder.

46
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,920
I'm beaten, I'm beaten.

47
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:36,200
After that, I started coming by to
visit the chief from time to time.

48
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:50,760
I thought she'd make the Olympics in judo, but now she's
settled down quietly as a wife in a wealthy Yamate family.

49
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,000
Is that so?

50
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:05,780
What's going on? When did she have all these kids?
They're not mine, hey, you lazy bum!

51
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:10,080
Anyway, Ryo-san, a rare visitor is here!

52
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:10,820
Hey!

53
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,960
A rare visitor, I tell you!

54
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,440
Senpai, you have a guest.

55
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,040
A guest?

56
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,320
For Ryo-chan.

57
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:20,200
Ryo-san.

58
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,420
It's been a long time.

59
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,120
Why, it's Yoko-chan!

60
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,060
Wow, it's been ages!

61
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:27,940
Yoko-chan?

62
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:32,240
Yeah, yeah. We were just talking
about you as we passed the tobacco shop.

63
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,980
You've changed so much.

64
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:37,120
Is something wrong?

65
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,840
No, it's nothing.

66
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:42,800
I just felt like seeing the Kameari
streets again after all this time.

67
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:46,620
I see. Your husband is a bigwig at Kasumigaseki,
isn't he?

68
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:47,660
Are you doing well?

69
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,920
Y-yes.

70
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:51,600
Don't tell me that just now was -

71
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,320
Yes, they're twins.

72
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:56,840
They're four now, but they're
already so mischievous it's exhausting.

73
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,580
Twins What are their names?

74
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,620
Kenji and Kouji.
Put together, we named them Kenkouji.

75
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:04,740
Kenji plus Kouji makes Kenkouji

76
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:06,780
Well, I guess I'll say that.

77
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,940
It really has been a long time

78
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:10,481
Nakagawa, Reiko,

79
00:05:10,531 --> 00:05:14,600
let me tell you about Yoko-chan
when she was in high school.

80
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,020
Stop it, Ryo-san.

81
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,700
Don't be shy, don't be shy.

82
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,720
Back then, at this police box,

83
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,820
there was me, the Chief, and Terai.

84
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:23,640
Totsuka was there too.

85
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:25,920
What?

86
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:27,640
Is that really true, Totsuka?

87
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,520
It's true, totally true.

88
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,280
I saw it with my own eyes.

89
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:34,400
Yoko-chan from that tobacco
shop has fallen in love?

90
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:36,440
It's spring

91
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,080
Here he comes, here he comes!

92
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,080
That's him.

93
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,900
Apparently he's a year ahead
of her in the literature club.

94
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:57,360
The literature club and judo club
don't exactly have much in common

95
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:01,120
Maybe that's why she's
never even spoken to him yet.

96
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:04,740
She just stares at him every
time until he walks past.

97
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:09,720
Right, let's somehow
arrange a date for them.

98
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,240
Hey, sorry, have you been waiting long?

99
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:18,320
N-no, I just got here.

100
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,720
Standing at attention

101
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,700
Just what you'd expect
from a sports club kid.

102
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:26,380
What was the sense of
guilt Raskolnikov felt,

103
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,760
don't you think it applies
to us high schoolers too?

104
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,140
Ah, y-yes.

105
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,440
What are you talking about?

106
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,060
I have no idea.

107
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:39,360
Well, a first date is
probably about like this.

108
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,200
Curry like that

109
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,620
The Snows of Kilimanjaro.

110
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,640
Aku Shoden.

111
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:51,140
I don't know why,
but I'm starting to feel sick.

112
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:53,060
This is a whole other world, isn't it.

113
00:06:53,060 --> 00:07:10,440


114
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:12,340
Are you trying to pick a
fight with me or something?

115
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,360
That's right, that's right!

116
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,200
Help me, Mommy!

117
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,480
Help, Mom?

118
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,640
So that's Mom over there?

119
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:30,620
Then Mom's going to
have to hang out with us.

120
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:32,040
This -

121
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,800
Are you looking to get hurt?

122
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:36,760
Alright?

123
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:37,900
Let's do this!

124
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:38,460
Totsuka!

125
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,500
Leave it to me!

126
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,520
Ryo-san, Totsuka-san!

127
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,420
I'm on your side, Yoko-chan!

128
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:05,020
Well done, Mom.
There are no more delinquents, right?

129
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:18,760
Mama's boy?

130
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,780
I don't know anything about it.

131
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:29,040
I've really learned that
being smart alone isn't enough.

132
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:30,800
That happened, didn't it?

133
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:34,480
After that,
the guy became smitten with Yoko-chan

134
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,120
and chased her relentlessly.

135
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,140
Unbelievable, isn't it?

136
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,760
Hey, wait up!

137
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,940
You shouldn't doodle on wanted posters.

138
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,360
Give back the handcuffs.

139
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:48,520
No matter how much you tell him,
he never listens.

140
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,520
Hey, Kenji! Koji!

141
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,620
Scolding them is pointless.

142
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:55,760
Kids this age are supposed
to get into mischief.

143
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,320
Hey, where's the handcuff key?

144
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,400
The two of them took that too.

145
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:05,840
What?

146
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:06,560
Uh...

147
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:18,300
Yes, yes, we all went to the sea together once, didn't we?
On the neighborhood association trip, to the Chiba beach, yeah.

148
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:28,220
So you two were her bodyguards, making sure no bad bugs got near our precious granddaughter.
Don't worry, it's fine.

149
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,000
Please look after Yoko.

150
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,060
We both have work to do, so...

151
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:34,120
Please.

152
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:37,260
Leave it to us.

153
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:39,660
I just can't put any effort into it.

154
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:40,400
I'm off.

155
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,040
How lovely!

156
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:10,000
Somehow, everyone looks scared.

157
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,916
It's fine, it's fine.

158
00:10:10,966 --> 00:10:14,420
We're just making sure no
bad bugs get near Yoko-chan.

159
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:17,500
Since we were entrusted with this,
we've got responsibilities.

160
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,140
This is fun!

161
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:33,460
Hey, Ryo-san.

162
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,500
Well, when it comes to the sea,
this is what it's all about.

163
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,220
Ryotsu,
the waves are coming right up to you!

164
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,140
Knock it off already.

165
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,800
It's a beauty contest!

166
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:45,220
Reiko-chan, why don't you enter?

167
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:46,880
Me?

168
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:47,520
You'll be fine.

169
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,760
If we cheer you on, you're sure to win.

170
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:03,800
Next up, entry number 25!

171
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,900
Yoko-chan Sasaki from Katsushika Ward!

172
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,200
Here she is, Yoko-chan!

173
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,720
The tobacco shop princess!

174
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:40,680
Youth!

175
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,360
Boo! Boo!

176
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:51,020
Nobody said that!
Don't quietly hurl filthy heckles, you!

177
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:58,480
Fine, you lot, what class were you in? In middle school I was in Class B,
and I'm in Class C.

178
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,600
Nope, I won't be crushed!

179
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,940
I'm not doing romance!

180
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:04,040
Aaaaaah!

181
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:04,800
What a disaster!

182
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,580
Yeah!

183
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:07,700
Grrr!

184
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,280
Ugh!

185
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:11,740
Ugh!

186
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:11,980
Ugh!

187
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:12,480
Ugh!

188
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:12,820
Yaaah!

189
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,580
Grrr!

190
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:17,620
It always ends up like this!

191
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:22,420
Hey! Don't get it wrong!

192
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:24,100
We're police officers!

193
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,280
Don't lie!

194
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:27,280
Where do you find cops like you lot?

195
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,220
It's not a lie!

196
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,420
Alright, alright.

197
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,840
Listen to people!

198
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,540
If we were cops!

199
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:47,240
Ryo-chan, you haven't changed
at all since back then, have you?

200
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,660
That's true, very much like a senior

201
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,360
Alright, got it.

202
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,640
For a senior, you're taking a while.

203
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:57,660
Shut up, this wire is the tricky part.

204
00:12:59,420 --> 00:13:03,560
No, I'm sorry.
She really is a child who never listens.

205
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:14,280
She definitely takes after Mom, not Dad. Yeah,
the parts you'd hope to see of him aren't there, it's all the parts that aren't like him.

206
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:19,400
I wish Takashi-san could spend a
little more time with the kids too.

207
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:28,580
Come to think of it, so far the story has been all about Senpai and Totsuka,
and Terai hasn't shown up at all.

208
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:33,500
That's true. Hey, Ryo-chan,
do you have something about Terai and Yoko?

209
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:36,300
There's nothing like that.

210
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:40,360
But there is. Terai's special episode.

211
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:43,700
No, Ryo-san, you can't talk to that girl!

212
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:46,400
What, what, Ryo-chan? I want to hear!

213
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,640
Terai-san's up to something.

214
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,400
So what if it's not allowed?
It's already an accident, after all.

215
00:13:52,400 --> 00:14:02,800
Welcome! One pack of cigarettes, please.

216
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:09,100
Here's your usual, right?
Here's your usual. Thank you very much.

217
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:15,740
As expected of Super Electromagnet Robo!
Powerful magnet

218
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:22,200
Yo! What's up with Terai?
Liner cigarettes. He went out to buy some.

219
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:29,960
Five times... that's strange. Terai doesn't smoke, right?
He doesn't smoke, but he went out to buy some. It's the fifth time today!

220
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,980
Fifth time?

221
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:39,540
Terai! About those documents I left here...

222
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:47,580
Aaaaaah.

223
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:52,640
No way, ahaha.

224
00:14:55,160 --> 00:15:01,960
So Terai had a crush on Yoko.
He never managed to confess, though.

225
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:09,240
Don't joke around like that. Even if he had confessed,
he wouldn't have stood a chance, I bet.

226
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:15,420
She was dating her current husband anyway.
Come on, stop it.

227
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,860
And now Terai is surrounded
by his wife and two kids.

228
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:23,580
living a happy family life.

229
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:25,960
Time really flies, doesn't it.

230
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,600
Right, Yoko-chan.

231
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,660
Do you remember the wedding?

232
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,280
Yeah.

233
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:57,760
Grandma

234
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,291
Oh my,

235
00:15:59,341 --> 00:16:01,400
Yoko,

236
00:16:01,450 --> 00:16:03,560
what is it?

237
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:10,480
Grandma, thank you for looking
after me all these years.

238
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:13,860
What's gotten into you, all of a sudden?
That's not like you.

239
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:17,840
Such overly polite talk is bad for your health,
you know.

240
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,820
Well, I've always wanted to try it once.

241
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:24,140
Like in those TV dramas.

242
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:30,660
Honestly, it's amazing anyone was foolish
enough to take a tomboy like you as a bride.

243
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,900
I got my tomboyish side from you, Grandma.

244
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:36,420
Mom and Dad are both so quiet, after all.

245
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:41,020
Why, even I was demure and
ladylike back in the day,

246
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:43,860
they used to call me the Beauty of the Tobacco Shop,
you know.

247
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:46,980
Come on, I can't believe that.

248
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,980
A girl about to be married,
what's gotten into you?

249
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:52,060
That flippant way of talking

250
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:56,020
is fine,
I'm totally lovey-dovey with Takashi.

251
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,680
Even if you say that,

252
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,700
their family has been
respectable for generations.

253
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,580
The neighbors, unlike us downtown folks,

254
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:06,240
are the Yamanote wives, you see.

255
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:07,560
I see.

256
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:08,880
Yeah, that's right.

257
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,980
Because I don't want it
to turn into a hassle.

258
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,080
Maybe I'll just give up on getting married.

259
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:16,860
There you go again, saying things like that.

260
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,260
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

261
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:21,200
Make sure you go to your
husband's family properly.

262
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,180
I'll get along fine over there,
so don't worry.

263
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:25,700
Really, be dependable, okay?

264
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:27,740
Mm.

265
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:41,940
To think I'd get to see
Yoko in a bridal gown.

266
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:45,620
Now I have no regrets left, you know.

267
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:02,240
Grandma, you know where the place is, right?

268
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:07,240
The hotel, yes, I know.
Okay, I'll come along later.

269
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,020
You'd hardly recognize you.

270
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,140
You look too beautiful!

271
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:34,000
Well, as her guardian, I'm so proud.

272
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:41,080
There, all done!

273
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,800
That's it.

274
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,300
Right then.

275
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:49,560
Koharu-san.

276
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:50,940
Koharu-san.

277
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,060
Koharu-san.

278
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,080
Koharu-san.

279
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,860
Yes, this is Sasaki.

280
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,180
What?

281
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,560
Is it true, Dad?

282
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,140
Mr. Miyake next door just called.

283
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:09,600
Grandma.

284
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,960
How awful.

285
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:15,000
She was looking forward to seeing Yoko
in her bridal outfit more than anyone.

286
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:17,100
Dad.

287
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,280
No you don't!

288
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:27,840
Make sure nobody steals my beloved car,
you hear?

289
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:47,700
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah...

290
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:48,560
Let's go!

291
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:51,880
Move, move, move, move!

292
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:55,900
Come on, get out of the way!

293
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,320
Hurry up and get in!

294
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:03,120
Ryo-san!

295
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,300
Don't dawdle!

296
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:07,100
We've got to let Granny
see the bride in her outfit!

297
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:08,660
Yeah.

298
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:10,940
Here's a tip! Keep the change!

299
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,600
Here we go! Hold on tight!

300
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:15,360
Yeah!

301
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,000
Drift!

302
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:30,200
Damn it!

303
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:34,260
This way!

304
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:38,180
Dolly!

305
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:46,400
Ah -

306
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,560
Eeeeeeeh!

307
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:48,560
Aaaaaaah!

308
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:51,160
Damn it! Don't you dare die, Granny!

309
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:58,600
Granny!

310
00:20:59,000 --> 00:20:59,800
Grandma!

311
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:05,460
Are we too late?

312
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,300
Grandma!

313
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,540
Hang in there, Granny!
Pull yourself together!

314
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:14,460
Open your eyes! It's Yoko-chan!

315
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,440
Yoko-chan has come to help you!

316
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:18,440
We brought that female doctor to the shop!

317
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:22,220
Yoko-chan, take a look at her!
Don't die! Granny!

318
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,440
Will you all stop your noise already.

319
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:27,900
What do you mean,
"don't die"! That makes no sense!

320
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,600
Hmph.

321
00:21:28,980 --> 00:21:29,980
Ow ow.

322
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:34,100
Honestly, I'm not going to
die every time I get a bad back!

323
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:37,060
A bad back? Lumbago?

324
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,380
No, ugh, aaah...

325
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:41,220
Ah, that, oh my...

326
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,940
What are you doing?

327
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,060
What about the wedding?

328
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,760
Don't tell me the groom ran away on you...

329
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:51,100
No, no.

330
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:53,120
Don't worry.

331
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:55,200
Look at me.

332
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:57,660
I wanted Grandma to see me like this.

333
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:58,540
That's why.

334
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:01,980
Yoko...

335
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,560
You're a beautiful bride.

336
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,640
Yoko.

337
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:11,060
I think I understand you well.

338
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:13,260
And you're the one who chose him.

339
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:15,980
He's definitely the world's greatest angel.

340
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:17,460
Alright?

341
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,920
No matter what happens, don't let go of him.

342
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:22,440
Mm.

343
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:28,520
Hurry back! The bride is waiting to see you.

344
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:30,680
Yeah! Ryo-san, I'm counting on you again.

345
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:57,460
I wonder if she had a
fight with her husband.

346
00:22:57,460 --> 00:22:58,720
Probably.

347
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:00,800
I wonder what the cause was.

348
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:03,740
Whatever the reason, it doesn't matter.

349
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:08,360
Kameari may have changed,

350
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:10,380
but people's hearts haven't.

351
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,780
They should have gone back to the
feelings they had when they first met.

352
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:21,240
Granny's probably pleased about
it from beyond the grave, too.

353
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:23,100
I'm still alive, you know!

354
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,240
Whoa, I was joking!

355
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:28,220
Granny's as lively as ever.

356
00:23:28,620 --> 00:23:29,880
Of course she is.

357
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:32,140
But you're retiring from
the tobacco shop, right?

358
00:23:32,140 --> 00:23:34,800
Retire? Don't talk nonsense.

359
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:37,280
What do you think will be built here?

360
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:39,740
I'm the owner, you know.

361
00:23:39,740 --> 00:23:41,700
It used to be a tobacco shop, once.

362
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:45,220
I'm not dying until my
granddaughter gets married.

363
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:53,820
We were invited to an event where
the Orient Express runs in Japan.

364
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:58,960
But inside that moving locked room,
Mrs. Christie's ring was stolen.

365
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:02,520
Alright, this is where I,
Sherlock Ryotsu, come in!

366
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:05,540
Next time: The Orient Express Theft Case.

367
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:07,160
The culprit is you!

368
00:24:11,660 --> 00:24:13,900
Surely, there's Kameari!

369
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:19,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

370
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:20,760
Thank you.

